    [
     1,
     "Unless you want to do that for commercial purposes, I&#39;d rather drop a few lines of jQuery to hit OpenCPU HTTP API via CORS/JSONP and return output in an user-friendly format. Rolling your own interface will be pain in the @$$, or a good practice, depending on your needs/skill level.<br>\r\n\r\n<br>See docs for details: <a href=\"https://public.opencpu.org/pages/docs.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://public.opencpu.org/pages/docs.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793239624782000&amp;usg=AOvVaw31_0bYiTFb-ihtOkEigoo_\">https://public.opencpu.org/pages/docs.html</a><br><br>Otherwise, RApparmor, sandboxR, just like Gergely suggested... oh, and... good luck! =)<br>\r\n\r\n<br>OR, something like this even: <a href=\"http://code.google.com/p/renjin/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://code.google.com/p/renjin/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793239624782000&amp;usg=AOvVaw30LaDTBBTMspkZCH1yGJ9Y\">http://code.google.com/p/renjin/</a><br clear=\"all\"><br>aL3xa"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<br><br>\r\n<br><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Mon, Oct 8, 2012 at 8:47 PM, Daróczi Gergely <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">ger...@snowl.net</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\">\r\n\r\n<font color=\"#663333\"><font><font face=\"verdana,sans-serif\">Hello,</font></font></font><div><font color=\"#663333\"><font><font face=\"verdana,sans-serif\"><br></font></font></font></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(102,51,51);font-family:verdana,sans-serif\">to run R commands in a browser, you could setup a non-interactive console with even a simple textarea or you may look for a nifty JS library. This can be addressed quite easily I suppose.</span></div>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div><font color=\"#663333\"><font><font face=\"verdana,sans-serif\"><br></font></font></font></div><div><font color=\"#663333\"><font><font face=\"verdana,sans-serif\">But you should be familiar with securing/hardening your newly installed system, and take this serious :)</font></font></font></div>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div><span style=\"font-family:verdana,sans-serif;color:rgb(102,51,51)\">I really suggest you to check out e.g. </span><a href=\"https://github.com/jeroenooms/RAppArmor\" style=\"font-family:verdana,sans-serif\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/jeroenooms/RAppArmor&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793239624782000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2mh4zvIWJ1HJS69I_4g-k7\">RApparmor</a><span style=\"font-family:verdana,sans-serif;color:rgb(102,51,51)\"> and </span><a href=\"https://github.com/Rapporter/sandboxR\" style=\"font-family:verdana,sans-serif\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/Rapporter/sandboxR&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793239624782000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3G4K0weFGxLJCXnwvoR-1F\">sandboxR</a><span style=\"font-family:verdana,sans-serif;color:rgb(102,51,51)\"> packages. I have created a simple webapp for the latter, you might be interested: </span><a href=\"http://sandboxr.no-ip.org/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://sandboxr.no-ip.org/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793239624782000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3A4PgrCfNRhUWkfC7eDzXw\">http://sandboxr.no-ip.org/</a></div>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div><span style=\"font-family:verdana,sans-serif;color:rgb(102,51,51)\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:verdana,sans-serif;color:rgb(102,51,51)\">Best,</span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:verdana,sans-serif;color:rgb(102,51,51)\">Gergely</span></div>\r\n\r\n<div><div>\r\n\r\n<div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Mon, Oct 8, 2012 at 7:51 PM, lex ter <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">lex...@googlemail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\">\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">Hello Everybody,<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">I finally have installed rApache on an Ubuntu (also thanks\r\nto you help).<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">I wanted now to extend the site with a R console so that I\r\ncould use rApache as a connection point between R &lt;-&gt; Web<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">It should be something like (more or less^^)<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">R &lt;-&gt; rApache &lt;-&gt; Apache &lt;-&gt; Web &lt;-&gt;\r\nConsole<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Did anyone know how I could achieve that?<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Regards</p><